Resident colour/keying chain

Portions of the curve Hermite evaluator and basic spill subtraction are adapted
from EffectCraft, Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the EffectCraft contributors.
Pinned commit: ec7ced1f0515f0b6f376dbcc297f1c441f452d6e
Repository: https://github.com/storytold/effectcraft
Selected license: MIT (included as LICENSE.effectcraft).
The exact upstream files/hashes and adaptation boundaries are in sources.json.

Frameweave's existing compensated Float32 Pair arithmetic and Gaussian plan are
reused without introducing another device owner, Renderer or execution engine.
Levels, Channel Mix, normalized Unsharp, linear Cb/Cr-distance Key and smooth
Luma Key use the stated equations; they do not claim full EffectCraft/AE parity.
The Matte extension also adapts the min/max/axis selection from fx_color.wgsl,
util.rs morph_frac's full-2D fractional blend, and the normalized Matte Choker
ramp from fx_key.wgsl. Its three-sample interval decomposition and finite-canvas
contract are documented in MATTE.md. No full upstream choker/refiner is claimed.
No Rust binary, external framework or third-party runtime dependency is added.

The creative candidate adapts selected EffectCraft pointwise Tint/linear
Brightness-Contrast, Color Balance, six-hue Black & White, Tritone, hash_noise,
Sobel, CC Vignette and relief shading fragments at that same pinned commit.
Its HDR/PM/working-luma bridge and native centre-sampled Pixelate differ from
upstream display-clipped/thresholded variants. Exact originals, hashes, license
and per-fragment scope are under creative/vendor and creative/sources.json.

The blend candidate reuses ten separable equations and hard_light/blend_pixel
from that same archived common.wgsl. Its native-PM bridge, F32 opacity boundary,
signed HDR extension and zero-coverage emission policy are in blends/README.md;
blends/sources.json pins the exact original and the selected MIT license.

The foundations closure adapts additional blur sampling, threshold/posterize,
min/max, colour-selection masks and deterministic noise fragments from the same
MIT archive. foundations/sources.json records each extraction boundary; the
native continuous median, typed statistics/CDF, small convolution presets and
signed/HDR parameter extensions are documented in foundations/README.md.
